# NOTE: base .env / backend/.env / frontend/.env are INTENTIONALLY committed
# (see comment near line 39) — Emergent native deploy rewrites them at build time.
# Only .env.local / .env.*.local overrides are git-ignored.
#
# ⚠ If an automated env-manager re-adds the broad `.env` / `.env.*` /
# `*.env` patterns below this comment, the negation rules right after
# them will still keep the deploy-critical files tracked by Git.
.env
.env.*
*.env
# Force-include the three .env files that MUST be present in the deploy
# bundle. These negation patterns survive any automation that re-adds
# the wildcards above.
!/backend/.env
!/frontend/.env
!/.env
